.TH QDTEXT 1 "2026-05-02" "smartmet-textgenapps" "SmartMet Tools"
.SH NAME
qdtext \- generate natural-language weather forecasts from querydata
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qdtext
.RI [ options ]
.I configfile
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qdtext
reads querydata forecast files together with a configuration file and
produces natural-language forecast text using the SmartMet
.B textgen
library. It is used for generating area-specific forecasts (counties,
regions and similar) in multiple languages.
.PP
Output directory, areas to process and languages to use are normally
specified in the configuration file via the
.B qdtext::*
namespace and may be overridden on the command line.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h
Print the built-in help.
.TP
.B \-f
Create output directories if they do not exist (overrides
.BR qdtext::mkdir ).
.TP
.BI \-d " outdir"
Output directory (overrides
.BR qdtext::outputdir ).
.TP
.BI \-a " name1,name2,..."
Areas to process (overrides
.BR qdtext::areas ).
.TP
.BI \-l " lang1,lang2,..."
Languages to process (overrides
.BR qdtext::languages ).
.SH EXAMPLES
Run with a configuration file, generating Finnish and English forecasts
for two areas:
.PP
.RS 4
qdtext \-a kainuu,lappi \-l fi,en forecast.conf
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qdpress (1),
.BR qdarea (1),
.BR qdpoint (1),
.BR qdinfo (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Finnish Meteorological Institute
.PP
